      </div>
    </div>

    {# ── Buttons ── #}
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Buttons</h2>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:var(--space-md);align-items:center">
        <a href="#" class="btn btn--cta" onclick="return false">Primary CTA</a>
        <a href="#" class="btn btn--outline" style="color:var(--text-primary);border-color:var(--border-color)" onclick="return false">Outline</a>
        <button class="btn--nav-prev" style="position:static" disabled>Disabled</button>
        <button class="btn--nav-next" style="position:static" onclick="return false">Next</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# ── Lesson panel ── #}
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Lesson panel</h2>
      <p>The teacher's panel shows one step at a time. The cue tells the teacher whose turn it is; the boxes give the words, the action, the expected answer, the confirmation, and the correction. Confirmations are short and name the answer. There are no exclamation marks.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.625rem;max-width:40rem">
        <div class="tp-stepline"><span class="tp-cue tp-cue--model">My turn</span><span class="tp-cue tp-cue--lead">Together</span><span class="tp-cue tp-cue--test">Your turn</span><span class="tp-cue tp-cue--note">Set up</span></div>
        <p class="tp-say">Touch and count the apples.</p>
        <div class="tp-box tp-do"><span class="tp-label">Do</span><p>Watch that the child touches each picture once.</p></div>
        <div class="tp-box tp-answer"><span class="tp-label">Child</span><p>One, two, three, four, five, six.</p></div>
        <div class="tp-box tp-confirm"><span class="tp-label">If right</span><p>Yes.</p></div>
        <div class="tp-box tp-correct is-active"><span class="tp-label">If wrong</span><p>Stop. My turn. I touch each picture once and say one number for each. One, two, three, four, five, six. Your turn. Touch and count the apples.</p></div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:0.5rem"><button class="tp-btn tp-btn--error" type="button">Error</button><button class="tp-btn tp-btn--firm" type="button">Firm</button><button class="tp-btn tp-btn--next" type="button">Next</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# ── Visual aids ── #}
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Visual aids</h2>
      <p>Every picture on the child's screen is drawn by one renderer (assets/js/visuals.js) from plain data written in the curriculum. A sample:</p>
      <div class="sg-visuals" id="sg-visuals"></div>
    </div>
    <script src="/assets/js/visuals.js?v={{ build.version }}"></script>
    <script>
    (function () {
      var specs = [
        { t: "dots", n: 7, arr: "row" }, { t: "frame", size: 10, n: 7 }, { t: "obj", icon: "duck", n: 4 },
        { t: "eq", parts: [8, "+", 5, "=", "?"] }, { t: "family", a: 8, b: 5, c: 13, miss: "c" }, { t: "pv", tens: 3, ones: 4 },
        { t: "shape", s: "hexagon", c: "yellow" }, { t: "solid", s: "cube", c: "blue" }, { t: "clock", h: 4, m: 30 },
      ];
      var box = document.getElementById("sg-visuals");
      box.innerHTML = specs.map(function (s) { return '<div class="sg-visual">' + MDV.render(s) + "</div>"; }).join("");
    })();
    </script>

    {# ── Cards ── #}
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Cards</h2>
      <div class="guide-cards">
        <div class="guide-card"><h3 class="guide-card__title">Guide card</h3><p>Used on the guide and features pages for grouped information.</p></div>
        <div class="guide-card"><h3 class="guide-card__title">Another card</h3><p>Cards stack on narrow screens and form a grid on wider ones.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# ── Stats ── #}
    <div class="guide-section">
